{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 120,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Child] Look at that!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So pretty!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3090,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The other day my son asked me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4980,
    "dDurationMs": 1645,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why rainbows are curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6625,
    "dDurationMs": 995,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7620,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I could have given\nhim a simple explanation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10110,
    "dDurationMs": 2633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but instead I made this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12743,
    "dDurationMs": 1957,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14700,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With beautiful demonstrations\nI've never seen before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17250,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the perspective of a rainbow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18810,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a single raindrop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20130,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the best animations ever created"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22770,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the subject."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23603,
    "dDurationMs": 3907,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because I promise you, almost\nevery explanation out there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27510,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "double rainbow,\n(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29460,
    "dDurationMs": 1743,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is an oversimplification."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32550,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if raindrops\nspread white light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35520,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into colors like a prism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37260,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then why do you never see a rainbow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39270,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when looking in the direction of the sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41730,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or why is it darker above\na rainbow than under it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45570,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How can you make a rainbow\ndisappear with sunglasses?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49200,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's going on here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51420,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why is this rainbow so\nmuch smaller than usual?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54450,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how did this phenomenon\ndirectly lead to a Nobel Prize?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58590,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh yeah, we're going deep on this one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60510,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the full explanation\nis so much more satisfying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64020,
    "dDurationMs": 2493,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than anything you've seen before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67971,
    "dDurationMs": 1599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(rain splattering)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69570,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make a rainbow, you need three things,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72180,
    "dDurationMs": 3993,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raindrops, the sun and you, an observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77040,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, this is one of those\nexperiments that seems so simple,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80430,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I've never seen anyone do it before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83220,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have a glass sphere and\nthat represents my raindrop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87990,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because as we've learned\nin previous videos,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89910,
    "dDurationMs": 4015,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raindrops, of course, are\nessentially spherically shaped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93925,
    "dDurationMs": 1235,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(air whooshing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95160,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just preparing the particulate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96780,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that I can see the laser beams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99090,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over here I have a laser."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101580,
    "dDurationMs": 3423,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that laser beam\nrepresents a ray from the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106020,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rays of light from the sun\nreach a raindrop essentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108660,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parallel to each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109710,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the sun is so far away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113190,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When light strikes the sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115080,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of it reflects back\noff the front surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117810,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and some is transmitted into the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120540,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then at the back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121560,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again, some of the light\nreflects off the back surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124080,
    "dDurationMs": 1653,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and some is transmitted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126810,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every time light goes from\none medium into another,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129120,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of it will be reflected\nand some transmitted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132000,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And exactly how much depends\non the angle of the light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134850,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its polarization and the\nnature of the two media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138150,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is actually helpful here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139770,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because I can use the reflections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141690,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make sure the laser\nis lined up properly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144360,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think I've got this red laser lined up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145890,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's hitting the middle of the sphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147810,
    "dDurationMs": 1088,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's reflecting here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148898,
    "dDurationMs": 2212,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but some of the light goes through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151110,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and some of the light\nreflects at the back surface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153420,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then some of the light\ngoes through for the wall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156420,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I'm going to keep the laser horizontal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158700,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and move it up the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161160,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's call the distance\nfrom the central axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163560,
    "dDurationMs": 1932,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the impact parameter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165492,
    "dDurationMs": 948,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(rhythmic music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166440,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As I move the laser up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167700,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the reflection off the\nfront surface goes up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170940,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just bouncing off that curve surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173700,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I can tell you,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174780,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is a simple, boring reflection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177420,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nothing interesting happens with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179190,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not involved in\nrainbows, so it's there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182280,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we're basically going to ignore it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184020,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the rest of the video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185730,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's much more interesting\nis the reflection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187920,
    "dDurationMs": 1473,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off the back surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190410,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now here comes that ray here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192210,
    "dDurationMs": 1863,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this spot is on the table."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195330,
    "dDurationMs": 3573,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the laser moves up, it goes down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200730,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the whole beam\ninside the sphere bends down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204660,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because as the\nlight enters the sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206970,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it slows down, and so it refracts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211920,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why does light slow\ndown when it enters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214020,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a dense medium like glass?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215850,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I think a lot of people can tell you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217590,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that light is an electromagnetic wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219540,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without really thinking\nabout what that means."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222480,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know the electric field\naround a charged balloon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225240,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that pulls on your hair or\nmakes it stick to a wall"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228630,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the magnetic field around a bar magnet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230940,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that makes iron filings line up?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233220,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, light is what happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234840,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you could rip the electric\nfield off the charges,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238080,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic field off the\nmagnet, smoosh them together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241620,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and send them out traveling\nthrough space, sort of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244890,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean in practice,\nelectromagnetic waves are made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247410,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by accelerating charges like\nby wiggling them up and down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251640,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the changing electric and\nmagnetic fields, they create,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254310,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "team up as light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255600,
    "dDurationMs": 1593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and head off on their own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259110,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The clearest explanation I know of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260730,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for how light is slowed down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262050,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a medium comes from\nGrant over at 3Blue1Brown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265590,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I asked him if I could\nsummarize his explanation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267660,
    "dDurationMs": 2643,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for this video and he graciously agreed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271260,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when those electromagnetic\nwaves encounter charges"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274440,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a medium like those in the\nfirst layer of our sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277650,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the light pushes them back and forth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280380,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of each charge\nas a little mass on a spring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283650,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the changing electric\nand magnetic fields cause it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286080,
    "dDurationMs": 2883,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to vibrate at the same\nfrequency as the light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289980,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now you have wiggling\nthat is accelerating charges."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they too must create their\nown electromagnetic waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298680,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the net electromagnetic\nfield is just a sum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301770,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the incident wave plus this new wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305550,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The result is almost exactly\nlike the original wave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309720,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except it has shifted back slightly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311970,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It receives a phase kick"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314310,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and each layer of the material\nadds another phase kick."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317790,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the net effect of all\nthis is the wavelength"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319950,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the radiation decreases\nin the new medium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323130,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since the frequency stays the same,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325860,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a shorter wavelength\ndecreases the speed of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328770,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the material."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330270,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The speed of light in a vacuum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331440,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the speed of\nlight in a medium is called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333660,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the refractive index."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335340,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's around 1.5 for\nglass and 1.33 for water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340080,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when light enters a\nnew medium at an angle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343440,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the part of the wave crest that\nenter the new medium first,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346890,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slow down first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348360,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this changes the angle\nof all the wave crests."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352380,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since the direction of a\nbeam of light is perpendicular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355350,
    "dDurationMs": 3873,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the wave crests, this means\nthe light changes direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360390,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to recap, light\ncauses charges to wiggle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363480,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they create their own\nelectromagnetic wave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366090,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which gives the light a phase\nkick shortening its wavelength"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369780,
    "dDurationMs": 3453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which slows it down and so it bends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374370,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a simple mathematical expression"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376200,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that relates the angles of\nincidence and refraction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378570,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the indexes of\nrefraction of the two media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381210,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's known as Snell's law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382890,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though it was\nindependently discovered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384690,
    "dDurationMs": 3582,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a handful of people,\nsome well before Snell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388272,
    "dDurationMs": 1488,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389760,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what we're\nseeing in the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392250,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The higher the laser hits the sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394290,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the larger the angle of incidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396000,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hence the more it bends\ndown due to refraction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399420,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of this light exits\nout the back of the sphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402060,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but some of it is reflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404100,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's this reflected ray"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405930,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we can see coming out\nthe front of the sphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407790,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "below the incident beam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409860,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I wanna graph the\nangle of this reflected ray"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412950,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as I move the beam up the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415260,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the laser is dead center,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417210,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the reflected beam comes\nstraight back at the source."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420090,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's call that 0 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422550,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then as I move the laser\nup, this angle increases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426420,
    "dDurationMs": 3507,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the light's coming back at\n5 degrees, then 10 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429927,
    "dDurationMs": 3096,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it keeps increasing the higher I go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435240,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now we come to the critical point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437850,
    "dDurationMs": 1983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Watch this spot on the table."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440730,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As I move the incident beam\nup, this dot is moving in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444810,
    "dDurationMs": 3753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reflected ray is coming\ncloser and closer and closer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449670,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's a certain point right there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452730,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it stops coming closer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455910,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look at that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457680,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even as I keep moving\nthis beam higher and higher,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460620,
    "dDurationMs": 2314,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it doesn't get any closer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462934,
    "dDurationMs": 1316,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464250,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then it goes back the other way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469020,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what we're seeing\nthere is a maximum angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472410,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this reflected ray reaches\nbefore it turns around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475530,
    "dDurationMs": 1833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and goes back the other way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478765,
    "dDurationMs": 1145,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479910,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is really important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482430,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It means that over a range\nof impact parameters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485430,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a range of heights of the laser,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487380,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the reflected beam comes out\nat essentially the same angle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491610,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means the light\nis becoming concentrated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495090,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at that angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496470,
    "dDurationMs": 3213,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a concentration of light\nrays is called a caustic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501480,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Curved surfaces all\ntend to create caustics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504270,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from coffee mugs to glasses\nor even just rippling water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508170,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Caustics create the light patterns we see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510330,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by concentrating light rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512640,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the case of red light\nthrough a sphere of water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514980,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the maximum scattering angle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516780,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hence this caustic\nalways occurs at 42 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520950,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "below the horizontal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522810,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since my sphere is made of\nglass rather than water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, the angle is different,\nbut the principle is the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530670,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you might ask, why does\nthis reflected ray reach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533700,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a maximum angle and then turn around?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536280,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the answer is just geometry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538770,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As I move the laser up the sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540810,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "although the ray refracts down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542670,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the point on the back of the sphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544230,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it reflects continues to move up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547110,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until you get to this special point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549630,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is about 7/8 the\nradius of the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553170,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here, the angle of\nincidence is so steep"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556530,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the refracted ray stops\nhitting the back higher"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559080,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and starts hitting it lower."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561180,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is why the reflection turns around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564150,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore we get a\nmaximum scattering angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567270,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the concentration of\nlight rays at that angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570900,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the precise maximum\nscattering angle depends"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573840,
    "dDurationMs": 1203,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the color of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576600,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see why, let's go back\nto the idea of the charges"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579120,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the sphere as masses on springs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581670,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a natural frequency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583590,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a frequency at which they would oscillate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585270,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if not driven at any particular frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588270,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in most materials,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589350,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this natural frequency is pretty high,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591510,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much higher than the\nfrequencies of visible light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594540,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, when light pushes\na charge back and forth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597330,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the amplitude of the\nresulting vibration depends"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600450,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the difference between\nthe frequency of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602670,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the natural frequency of the charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604950,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The closer the two frequencies are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606870,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the greater the amplitude\nof the resulting vibration,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609870,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which makes sense if you've\never pushed someone on a swing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612660,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The closer your pushing frequency is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614700,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the natural frequency of the swing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616680,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the higher they'll go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618840,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that higher\nfrequency light like blue light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will cause the charges to\nwiggle with greater amplitude."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625680,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because of this, the charges produce"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627870,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher amplitude\nelectromagnetic radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630510,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which creates a bigger phase kick,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632760,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which shortens the wavelength\nproportionally more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635610,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making higher frequency\nlight travel slower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638550,
    "dDurationMs": 2793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and bend more than lower frequency light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642330,
    "dDurationMs": 2493,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right, I'm gonna change lasers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645930,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when I repeated the\nexperiment with green light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648330,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it refracted more than red light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650370,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore the green\ndot turned around sooner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652770,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the red dot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654090,
    "dDurationMs": 1833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whoa, oh,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656940,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's the minimum deflection for green"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660300,
    "dDurationMs": 2703,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's significantly\ndifferent than for red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663930,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, its maximum\nscattering angle was smaller"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667470,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than for red light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668880,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the sphere were water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669960,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would occur at around 41\ndegrees below the horizontal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673380,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, for blue light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674730,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the maximum scattering\nangle approaches 40 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678540,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I do have a specialty laser,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680220,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is very bright blue,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682530,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's very dangerous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683610,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we're gonna use it very carefully."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686760,
    "dDurationMs": 2203,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how are we gonna use it\nvery carefully, Derek?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688963,
    "dDurationMs": 1457,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(tool thuds)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690420,
    "dDurationMs": 1184,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a good question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691604,
    "dDurationMs": 1006,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(tape ripping)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692610,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe we're just gonna tape it on here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696229,
    "dDurationMs": 982,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697211,
    "dDurationMs": 2667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(playful music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706089,
    "dDurationMs": 4611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the blue only makes it to\nthere, green here, red to here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710700,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it is a pretty serious spread here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713490,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think my experiment may\nbe a little wonky honestly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717240,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think this one wasn't\nperfectly horizontal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720720,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To really see the\nimportance of the caustic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723450,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imagine we illuminate the\nsphere uniformly with red light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727260,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, more light is\ngoing to hit the sphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729060,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at higher impact parameters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730980,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the further out you go,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732420,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more area there is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734430,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I've adjusted these sections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736470,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that they all have the same area."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739170,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then using our graph of\nthe scattering angle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741630,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can see where all of\nthis red light will end up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744300,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after reflecting off the back surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746880,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of it ends up at the\nmaximum scattering angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750570,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make this more obvious,\nwe can add more light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753840,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we can do the same\nthing for orange and yellow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758100,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all of the other colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761490,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what gives us the rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764300,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft choral music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766650,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not enough to say that a\nraindrop spreads white light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769170,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into its component colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770820,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because all of the light that hits closer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772440,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the middle is spread too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774480,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But since the reflections\nall overlap as they come out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777360,
    "dDurationMs": 2493,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the colors mix and produce white again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780690,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's only the difference in\nmaximum scattering angles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783690,
    "dDurationMs": 3368,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the caustics they produce\nthat gives us the rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787058,
    "dDurationMs": 2417,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791340,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now we know what happens\nalong a single radius"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793920,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794940,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happens if we uniformly illuminate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798000,
    "dDurationMs": 2393,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the whole sphere with white light?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800393,
    "dDurationMs": 1687,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(bright music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802080,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I blacked out my window"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803250,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and cut a hole just big\nenough for afternoon sunlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806310,
    "dDurationMs": 1173,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cover the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810150,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see there's a circle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812250,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of white light coming from the reflections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814560,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off the back of the sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816210,
    "dDurationMs": 3753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then around it, there's\na ring of rainbow colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822420,
    "dDurationMs": 903,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Come on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824580,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One raindrop creates a cone of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The inside is all white,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830400,
    "dDurationMs": 2913,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the ring around\nthe outside is colored."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834570,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the perspective of a\nrainbow from a single raindrop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838830,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All these different light rays coming in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840450,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at different places reflect\nback off the front surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843420,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the back surface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844463,
    "dDurationMs": 2707,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that reflection off the\nback surface reaches"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847170,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a maximum angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849000,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for blue, green, yellow, and red,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852180,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the maximum angle is different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854340,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the red maximum angle is the furthest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856650,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why it's on the outside here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858510,
    "dDurationMs": 2254,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So good, so good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860764,
    "dDurationMs": 1526,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862290,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What I really wanted to see\nis if I could observe the cone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865800,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of different colored caustics\nthat produced that ring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869160,
    "dDurationMs": 1636,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ho, ho, ho, ho, ho, ho, ho,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870796,
    "dDurationMs": 1604,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ho, ho, ho, ho."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872400,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You've got to see this color cone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874620,
    "dDurationMs": 1563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have got to see this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877680,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My eye is right in the color cone here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879870,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can see the color cone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881100,
    "dDurationMs": 843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is so cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882977,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885397,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is the crazy focus\non the back of the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891540,
    "dDurationMs": 3948,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you stick your finger in\nthere, it gets burnt very quick."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895488,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ow!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896321,
    "dDurationMs": 1719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That thing is a focal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899498,
    "dDurationMs": 1879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901377,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this really looks like a rainbow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903510,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but remember, this is\njust the light coming away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905760,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a single droplet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907530,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you see a rainbow, there\nare billions of raindrops,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910500,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and each one is projecting a rainbow cone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913110,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back toward the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914970,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how does all of this create\na single unified rainbow?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920370,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, for your eye to see a color,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922200,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's pick red in a\ncertain part of the sky,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925230,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the red caustic from a\nraindrop there must go directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928830,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into your eye."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930330,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this only happens when\nthe angle from the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933180,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the raindrop to your eye is 42 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937410,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this explains why rainbows\ntake the form of an arch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940920,
    "dDurationMs": 1591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a 42 degree angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942511,
    "dDurationMs": 2729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(intense music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945240,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the violet light from these\nsame raindrops passes above"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948720,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or beside your eye, so\nyou can't possibly see it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952410,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are raindrops below"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954960,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and inside the arc of\nthose red giving raindrops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958290,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whose violet caustics\ndo intersect your eye."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961860,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They form a shallower angle of 40 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964560,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between the sun and your eye."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966630,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, there are raindrops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968430,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at all intermediate angles that send you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970800,
    "dDurationMs": 2163,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the other colors of the rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974130,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a rainbow really is the\nultimate optical illusion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977940,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from billions of droplets each\nprojecting a rainbow cone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982350,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see a single static arch of color,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986220,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the droplets sending you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987450,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those colors are constantly changing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989790,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A single drop as it falls\nmight send to your eye"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992490,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first red, then orange,\nyellow, green, blue,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996570,
    "dDurationMs": 2113,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "indigo, and violet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998683,
    "dDurationMs": 1217,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999900,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because a rainbow must form\nan angle of 40 to 42 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003620,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with your eye,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004850,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the center of the arch must be on a line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007670,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that passes from the sun\nthrough the back of your head."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011420,
    "dDurationMs": 3813,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So your shadow is the\ncenter of your rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016100,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means no two people can ever see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018620,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the exact same rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020330,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, your left and\nright eyes don't even see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023150,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024380,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A rainbow is an optical\nillusion made unique"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028010,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for each perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030110,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This also explains why in\nmost parts of the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032330,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can only see a rainbow\nin the early morning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034910,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or late afternoon, not\nin the middle of the day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038750,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The higher the sun is, the\nlower the top of the rainbow is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042500,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when the sun is more than\n42 degrees above the horizon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045680,
    "dDurationMs": 3039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no rainbow is visible from the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048719,
    "dDurationMs": 2901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(water splattering)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051620,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even when rainbows are visible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053930,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can turn them\ninvisible using sunglasses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057440,
    "dDurationMs": 2553,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is as long as they are polarized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061130,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light from the sun is unpolarized,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063500,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means the electric fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1065120,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the light are all randomly oriented,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067640,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oscillating back and forth\nequally in all directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071360,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it just so happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073130,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that when the light in\nthe rainbow ray reflects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075590,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off the back of the droplet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077270,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it does so very close"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078800,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a special angle known\nas Brewster's angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1082390,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this angle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083690,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all light with its electric\nfield oriented parallel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086510,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the plane of reflection is transmitted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089600,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it passes out the back of the droplet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092510,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore the only light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094160,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is reflected has its\nelectric field perpendicular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097400,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the plane of reflection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099500,
    "dDurationMs": 2793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the light that\ncreates the rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103580,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means rainbow light is\npolarized along the direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107300,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the rainbow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108290,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so horizontal at the top"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109970,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and closer to vertical on the sides."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112640,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why you can\nuse a polarizing filter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115400,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make a rainbow disappear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117530,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or to make it brighter\nif you orient the filter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120470,
    "dDurationMs": 2613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to allow that polarized\nlight to pass through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124130,
    "dDurationMs": 3723,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why is it brighter under\na rainbow than above it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128720,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this is because the raindrops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130220,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beneath the rainbow are\nreflecting all colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132950,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of light at you off their back surfaces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135890,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what created the white disk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138140,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in my glass sphere experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140450,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, the raindrops above the top"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142880,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the rainbow are not\nreflecting any light to you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145400,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off their back surfaces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147020,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your eye is now outside the\nmaximum deflection angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150620,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of all of the colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153260,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you look up even further,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155570,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sometimes you see a second fainter rainbow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158300,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with its colors inverted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160280,
    "dDurationMs": 1867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Double rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162710,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So where does this come from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165140,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it comes from an\nadditional reflection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167510,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside the raindrops."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169190,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, instead of reflecting once"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170810,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off the inside of the sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172250,
    "dDurationMs": 1581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light reflects twice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173831,
    "dDurationMs": 3219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These reflections also\ncreate colored caustics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177050,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though much fainter because light is lost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179210,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with each reflection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181040,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at deflection angles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182900,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this light starts going out\nthe back of the raindrop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185330,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at an angle of 180 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187550,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the further out light\nhits from the center,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1190130,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the smaller the angle\nlight reflects back at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193040,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until it reaches a minimum\nof around 50 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196730,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for red light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198170,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then it turns around and\ngoes back the other way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201560,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So between 42 and 50 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204260,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is dark because no light\nreflected once or twice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208040,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside a raindrop comes out at this angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211790,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as Alexander's Dark Band."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215840,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, there is photographic evidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217640,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of third and fourth order rainbows formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220130,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after three or four internal reflections,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223460,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this light comes out\nthe back of a raindrop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226070,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they are the only kinds of rainbows"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228800,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you could expect to see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229850,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when looking in the direction of the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232400,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they're so faint"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233660,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that conditions would have to be perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236120,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Under lab conditions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237230,
    "dDurationMs": 3393,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to 200th order rainbows\nhave been detected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1241820,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that is not what is going on here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244820,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as a supernumerary rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248720,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Multiple rainbow like bands\nshow up under a primary rainbow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253250,
    "dDurationMs": 1061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this only occurs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1254311,
    "dDurationMs": 2509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the raindrops are all really small,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256820,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just 10ths of a millimeter in diameter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260030,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the light rays that\npassed just above and below"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1262580,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the primary rainbow ray end up coming out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265160,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at similar angles under 40 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268190,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they travel slightly\ndifferent distances"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270740,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the order of a wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272930,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because of this, those\nlight rays can interfere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275240,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "constructively and destructively,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277460,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "producing a series of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279200,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and dark bands inside the main rainbow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1282380,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Different colors in these\nsupernumerary rainbows overlap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285980,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than in the main rainbow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287960,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they can produce strange\ncolors like magenta,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290930,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a combination of blue and red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1293900,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Supernumeraries also offer a clue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296360,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to how these small rainbows work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299270,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whenever I saw images like this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301010,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even observed this sort\nof thing from an airplane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304040,
    "dDurationMs": 3502,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I wondered how a rainbow\ncould be so small."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1307542,
    "dDurationMs": 1628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft choral music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309170,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are known as\nglories or Brocken bows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312500,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of the usual 42 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314690,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these circles of color are only around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316850,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two to four degrees wide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1319160,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the key is that just\nlike in supernumeraries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322100,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "glories are due to interference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1324560,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they too require tiny water droplets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1327590,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just 10ths of a millimeter in diameter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330260,
    "dDurationMs": 3963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are the sorts of droplets\nyou'd find in fog or clouds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1335780,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light that strikes the edge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337820,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the drop can go around the back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340340,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and come straight back at the source."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1343100,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see that with the\nlaser on the glass sphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346490,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but effectively in the presence\nof parallel light rays,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350150,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tiny little droplets become\na ring source of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354350,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for these tiny droplets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356240,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the distance from one point to all edges"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1359960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the sphere can vary on\nthe order of a wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1364280,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So take for example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365330,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the point right out in front of the drop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367490,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, now the distance\nto all edges is the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370550,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the light interferes\nconstructively here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1372800,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and produces a bright spot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374780,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a little bit off to one side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1377000,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and now half of the light, on average,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1379550,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has traveled an extra half a wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1381770,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we get a dark spot here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1384170,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you go a little further,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1385790,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well now the light has traveled\nan extra whole wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388430,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now the light is\narriving in phase again,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1390680,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we get a bright spot here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392720,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we can rotate this around 360 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395990,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and extend it out in all directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397850,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what we get is a\nfuzzy bullseye pattern."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401480,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, all the different colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1403040,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of light have different wavelengths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404540,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1405373,
    "dDurationMs": 2377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bullseye patterns aren't\ncompletely overlapping."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407750,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when they're superimposed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1409370,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we see is rings of color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413660,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is just the pattern\nfrom a single droplet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416300,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but just like with a rainbow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1417770,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you have millions or\nbillions of these droplets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420440,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all contribute to\nproduce this same pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1423380,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with your shadow at the center."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426549,
    "dDurationMs": 1091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(soft music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427640,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it was just such a\npattern that inspired"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1430220,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Nobel Prize winning discovery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432920,
    "dDurationMs": 1478,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In September of 1894,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1434398,
    "dDurationMs": 4132,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a scientist named CTR Wilson\nwas visiting an observatory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1438530,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the Scottish Hills."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440450,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was then that he observed\n\"the coloured rings surrounding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444230,
    "dDurationMs": 2637,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the shadow cast on mist or cloud.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448010,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He recalls that these glories,\n\"greatly excited my interest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1451850,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and made me wish to imitate\nthem in the laboratory.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455720,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Wilson invented the cloud chamber"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1459380,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the explicit purpose\nof observing glories."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463550,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, once he\ndiscovered the cloud chamber,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1465410,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made the tracks of\nenergetic particles visible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467870,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he abandoned his original aim"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1470150,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and was later awarded the Nobel Prize."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473300,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it all started with the\nmystery of rings of color"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1477230,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the fog."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481379,
    "dDurationMs": 1251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Child] Wow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1482630,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wow, looks so nice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1484490,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How did you see that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486400,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now I hope you know my\nson, why rainbows are curved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491150,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and why they're polarized\nand why they exist at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1494930,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even more than that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496220,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I hope you know why I find such enjoyment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1498770,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in learning about our world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500810,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why it is worth figuring things out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503930,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For millennia, rainbows have been this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506540,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blatant challenge held up to us by nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509870,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But can you figure this out?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512030,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's satisfying to say we have."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1515450,
    "dDurationMs": 2805,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Child] I'm looking at a\ndifferent rainbow than you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518255,
    "dDurationMs": 1091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519346,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(celestial music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523370,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I started researching this video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524990,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I thought I already knew about rainbows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1527540,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, I'd learned all of the colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529490,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the rainbow in school"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530840,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that it was caused by light\nrefracting and reflecting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1534530,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I realized now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1535880,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I'd only really just\nmemorize things about rainbows"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1538820,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and not really understood how they work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541580,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learning should be about\nmastering a subject,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1544040,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not memorizing a list of facts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546320,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why we asked\nBrilliant to sponsor this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549290,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, Brilliant helps\nyou become smarter every day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1551960,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with quick interactive\nlessons on everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554090,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from math and science to data analysis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556760,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "programming, AI, you name it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1558890,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what makes Brilliant\nso effective is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1561350,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you learn by doing and getting hands on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564530,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
